WEBVTT

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.400
Geez, give me a break.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.860
I can't drink any more of that virility drink.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.370
It's only 6 AM.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.490
Yes, this is Mikadono.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.580
Good morning, Onii-sama!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.660
It's already morning.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.040
Please get up.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.040
You!

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.030
It seems you've only just realised it.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.880
I'm your little sister!

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.190
Do you remember that time when you met me at Kumagorou's funeral service?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.810
As I thought, you were the one who said you were my little sister back then.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.960
Yep.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.810
I'm always thinking about you, Onii-sama.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.820
So much that I'm giving you this morning wake-up call.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.470
It's still 6 AM.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.090
It's healthy to go to bed early and wake up early.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.440
Didn't the school principal say that before in a pep talk?

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.330
How would you know something like that?

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.080
Naturally, because I go to the same school as you do.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.840
I'm worried about you, Onii-sama.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.380
How many days have you been late because you've stayed up too late?

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:19.140
Living by yourself because you want to be able to buy as much porn as you like...

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.140
Coping with that every night is bad for your body.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.350
I was doing homework!

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.730
You even know about my private life?

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:35.490
It's okay to be vigorous, but I'm worried that when
the time comes for us to get married, you'll have dead wood.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.900
What kind of a worry is that?

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:40.900
In the first place, I'm not going to marry you.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.910
That's not possible, Onii-sama.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.870
You're definitely destined to marry me.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.000
Well then Onii-sama, have a good day.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Hey, wait!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.310
Since I got woken up so early, I'm still sleepy.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.620
Konoe?

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.250
Why are you here?

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.980
Good morning.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.520
Since I woke up a little earlier than usual,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.240
I thought maybe I should go to school with you.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.780
Woke up early...

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.910
What's wrong, Shougo-san?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.720
You seem a little dazed.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:53.280
Ah, no...

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.680
It's nothing.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.170
Also, you were up late, weren't you?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.670
<i>Coping with that every night is bad for your body.</i>

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.800
N-No.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.840
It's not like I cope with that every night.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:05.630
Eh?

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.680
Cope with?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.990
It's nothing.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:08.520
Really.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.890
It's nothing.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.100
You seem strange, Shougo-san.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.640
Your eyes seem bloodshot.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.100
Did you not get enough sleep?

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.860
I'll be awake by the time we get to school.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.570
If you go to class with that sleepy face, the teacher will be angry with you.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.610
As the class rep, I can't overlook that.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.580
How was that?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.900
Are you awake now?

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.420
W-What are you doing all of a sudden?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:39.670
Watching the academy students' daily life is also part of the class rep's job.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:42.970
My new car is a...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.300
What kind of a class rep is that?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.760
But, if I were to marry Konoe...

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.100
It would be like that every morning.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.770
No, even better than that.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.270
Congratulations!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.690
Mikadono-senpai, congratulations!

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.030
Konoe-chan, congratulations!

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.780
Konoe, is it okay?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.010
Konoe, I love you.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.290
I will never let you go.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.040
Me neither.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.040
Because I'm Shougo-san's...

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.540
...little sister!

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:25.550
What?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.430
You got another phone call from your little sister?

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:29.940
Yeah.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.710
So, is it Tsuruma-kun again?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.390
I thought so for a moment, but I don't think that's right.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:42.770
But, it shouldn't be possible to reproduce that voice
without the voice changer in Tsuruma-kun's cell phone.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:45.740
Looking at it this way, the new little sister's identity must be her.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.730
Don't you think that's a little strange?

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.570
Strange?

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.450
If she did it like this, then it would certainly be suspicious.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.500
Don't you think it's strange to do something like that?

00:05:55.700 --> 00:06:00.130
It could be a trick to fool you into thinking she isn't suspicious.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.170
But let's assume there's a third party for now.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.880
How would they be able to replicate that little sister voice?

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.390
Konoe's cell phone was a prototype model that was recalled before it went on sale, right?

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.390
That's it!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.390
If one of the prototypes of the phone was leaked...

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.310
There's no telling how many people could have one.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.470
It came to mind that if one such person used the cell phone's voice changer,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:28.450
they could take on the role of the unknown little sister.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.780
Speaking of which, after the last time there was an uproar over your little sister...

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.620
...you explained the situation to those who were involved, right?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.500
Yeah.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:42.000
The people involved being everyone who helped search for Konoe.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.130
Wait!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.640
That means,

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:49.130
the little sister could actually be one of those who were there, right?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.260
It would seem so.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.780
No way...

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.480
Well, it's not like that's already been decided.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:59.520
There's also the possibility that somebody
overheard that conversation from outside the room.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.790
Ah!

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.020
So this is where you were!

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.770
I was looking for you, Mikadono-senpai.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.530
I've been waiting for you, Mikadono Shougo.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.580
Um, what business does the head of the newspaper club have with me?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.080
This meeting must have been arranged by the hands of fate.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.210
It seems like you've appeared before me at last.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.130
I'm sorry.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.650
The club president, Araya-san,

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.260
is in the middle of acting out a second character.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:37.430
The only son of the former president of the Mikadono Group is
getting an extraordinary amount of admiration within this school.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.480
She's only in her second year, but the club president is already delusional.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.310
Sorry, but could you please go along with it for a little bit?

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:50.610
Therefore we, the "Miryuuin Times", are here to report the truth!

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.910
We must persevere to respond to the curiosity of the general public!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.490
Y-Yeah.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:06.540
The interview is about "The number one boy I want to be my Onii-chan, Mikadono Shougo"!

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.840
Um... can I go back now?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:18.680
Hello?

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.980
Good morning, Onii-sama.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.060
You're sleeping in late again today.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.480
I couldn't sleep because I was thinking about your identity.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.690
Oh my!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:32.900
You couldn't sleep last night because you were trying to imagine me doing unladylike things?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.830
Onii-sama is a pervert!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.250
Damn it... waking me up every single morning.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.000
Ah!

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.250
Geez, don't surprise me!

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.110
Why are you...?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.260
Why?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.760
Isn't it obvious I came to get you, Shougo?

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.090
There's something strange about you.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.140
You always seem to be in a daze.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:08:59.760
Yeah.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.680
Well, I haven't been getting enough sleep lately.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.060
Ah! I get it!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.390
You're doing perverted things until late at night, aren't you?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.080
You perverted, lecherous, child-making practice demon!

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.020
That's not it!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.280
More importantly, are you sure it's okay, Miyabi?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:13.280
Don't you have swimming club practice in the morning?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.610
Today is not a morning practice day.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.280
Swimming is after school.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:17.990
See?

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.490
I'm wearing a swimsuit, right?

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.160
What's with that? Don't surprise me like that.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.120
It looks like you woke up a little bit from that, just now.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.750
I'm awake, so you can cover it now.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.880
Ah! Sorry!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.530
Geez, Shougo.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.630
In a place like this...

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.840
You're so bold!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:39.540
Idiot!

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.800
What are you saying-

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:54.070
Somehow I made it through the morning, but if it stays like this...

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.070
Should I sleep in the infirmary during lunch break?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.320
Mikadono?

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.660
Sagara-senpai.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:03.740
What's wrong?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.330
Are you feeling sick?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.920
It's not that, but I haven't been getting enough sleep.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.340
So you were going to sleep in the infirmary?

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:15.710
But if you're going to take an afternoon nap, there's a better place.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.930
I was going to take a nap after this.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.300
Do you want to come, Mikadono?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.590
If there's a place I can sleep, it would be helpful,

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:25.810
but is it really okay if I come?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.730
I'll give you special permission to do so.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:31.860
However, after that you definitely have to come to my café.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.610
It's a promise, Onii-chan!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.740
Yeah.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.740
So, this is your hiding place?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.540
Nobody else knows about this place.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.540
It's a secret between the two of us.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.380
What exactly is this place?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:57.760
Originally, it was used to store equipment and research materials.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.840
There are also some exciting naughty magazines in here.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.010
What's that?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:06.830
Hey.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:07.700
Don't just stand around.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.680
Have a seat, Mikadono.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.270
Eh?

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.770
You came for an afternoon nap, right?

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:21.020
Um... You want me to sleep here, with you?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.350
Of course.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.530
If you sleep on the floor, your body will hurt.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.490
But there's not a lot of space...

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.230
That doesn't bother me.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.160
What is it?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.710
Are you being reserved because I'm your senior?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:32.920
It's not that.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.920
Don't worry, just because I'm your senior.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.680
I was born in March.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:42.380
So there isn't that much of a gap between our ages...

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.470
Really?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.930
I was born in April.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:47.970
So there's only a difference of about a month?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:51.730
Because of my birthday, I got moved up a year.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.980
Due to that mistake, I was put in the wrong class.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:55.980
Kuwabara, kuwabara.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.280
Why kuwabara?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.490
Shut up, Mikadono.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.570
You should hurry up and go to sleep, too.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:11.370
I can't sleep.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.930
There's no way I could sleep in this situation.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.530
Wow...

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.910
It's really messy here.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.660
But somehow, I have a feeling it's very like Sagara-senpai.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.790
Are these the "exciting naughty magazines"?

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.120
If I just have a peep...

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.100
No.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.970
It's bad to look at people's things without their permission.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.070
It's not something a future company president should do.

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:12.180
But a manager needs to be curious about things that they don't know about.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.250
No, no.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.390
But...

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.020
No...

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:30.950
eye catch

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.210
So the swimming club practises on Sundays, too...

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.240
She's taking her time...

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.490
Sorry for making you wait!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.370
You took your time, Miyabi...

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.950
It can't be helped, right?

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.450
I couldn't get a good time...

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.830
Anyway, let's go!

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.000
H-Hey!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.960
But why did you suggest that we go there together?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.670
It's fine, isn't it?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.880
Or is it that you don't want to go with me?

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.470
That's not the point.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.010
It should be around here somewhere...

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.480
Hey!

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.980
Lyrical Sisters...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.480
Are you sure you're okay with this?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:46.780
Hey, Miyabi-

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.660
Welcome home, Onii-chan!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.620
Welcome home, Onee-chan!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.660
O-Onii-chan...

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.580
Hey, hey, Shougo, did you hear that?

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.630
I'm a big sister!

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.460
Yep, it seems like it.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.630
A big sister... I'm a big sister!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.050
I'm Kurumi, a cheeky and slightly precocious little sister.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.260
Pleased to meet you!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.010
P-Pleased to meet you.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:18.020
Um...

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.770
What do they have on the menu?

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.320
A tsundere little sister's tsun tsun omelette rice...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.900
A spoilt little sister's sugary sweet sweet omelette rice?

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.200
Onii-chan, Onee-chan, what are your orders?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.700
I'd like a chocolate parfait.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.990
I'd like this "love omelette rice".

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:38.590
Eh?

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:39.850
Which one?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.000
I don't understand which one you mean by that!

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.500
Well, it's this "with utmost love omelette rice"...

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.090
Geez, Onii-chan!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.260
It's no good if you don't say the proper name from the menu!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.720
"The omelette rice which a clumsy little sister has made with utmost love!"

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:05.900
O-ni-i-cha-

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:06.820
Ah!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.900
There's no more space to write!

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.860
It says "Onii-cha!"

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.120
As long as you can eat it, it's fine!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.870
What's wrong, Onii-chan?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.030
What the hell...

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:24.290
This is extremely salty...

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.040
Eh?!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.130
Don't tell me... Perhaps...

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.550
Maybe I put in the wrong amount of salt again?!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.670
Maybe...?

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.720
Oh, Mikadono!

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.720
So you finally came to my café.

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:39.350
I did promise, right?

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:40.350
How is it?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.390
Has the moe killed you yet?

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.440
The moe hasn't killed me...

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.230
What?!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.570
To be unsatisfied with my café,

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.300
which has been called a treasure chest of moe!

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.630
As expected of Mikadono...

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.070
What a formidable guy.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:57.450
I'm going to carry on doing my best for you, Onii-chan!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.270
By the way, Senpai,

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:04.540
what's up with the way the waitresses in this café are dressed?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.670
In this café, they aren't waitresses, but <i>sisters</i>!

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.550
Today's the "Immature little sister wife day".

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:14.760
Having an immature little sister wife is today's taboo theme.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.640
A little sister as a wife...

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:29.980
Hello.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.360
Good morning, Onii-sama!

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.120
Who is it?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.740
It's Mikadono.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.040
May I have a nap in there again?

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.220
Sure.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.620
Come in!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.250
Onii-chan, welcome back, nyan~!

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.140
Hey, wait, wait!

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:04.390
Geez, I came here for a nap, but now my eyes are wide open.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.180
Sorry, sorry!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:10.960
I wanted to give the prototype ”cat's meow tail" a try.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:11.650
Right.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.030
Um, Senpai, may I ask you something?

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.110
Sure, ask whatever you want.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:20.730
Why are you running that café, Senpai?

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.290
I was an abandoned child.

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.640
Eh?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.390
I was found when I was around one or two years old.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:32.960
Even my name was given to me by the social services.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.530
So, about you being born in March...

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:41.220
I had many birthdays in that place.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.480
I've been good at mathematics ever since I was young.

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:49.310
I could even solve university level questions easily.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.360
My father, who was a university professor,

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:58.990
took custody of me and raised me, in order to expand on that ability.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.430
I've always thought you were amazing in a sense,

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.910
but you really are an amazing person.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.500
What do you mean by that?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.830
Eh? I was complimenting you, of course.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:15.380
My father went to the University of
Massachusetts to become a lecturer.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.430
The person who took care of me then was my mother,

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:22.010
who managed the coffee shop at that time.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:26.010
But after my mother fell sick and died, the shop was sold.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:29.730
I moved to Massachusetts, where my father was.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:37.320
But then, about two years ago, I made some money from papers I published under my father's guidance.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.150
And so I bought back my mother's shop.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:44.910
After all, there are memories of me and my mother in that shop.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:49.450
But it must have cost a lot of money to buy back the shop.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.410
What on earth was your paper about?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:59.630
Ah... If you're interested, then I'll show you the journal that published the paper.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:03.390
I'm sure it was around here somewhere...

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.100
Oops...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:09.640
Are you all right?

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:10.890
Yep.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:11.980
I'll give you a hand.

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:24.410
As I thought, if I don't organise things a bit, it could be bad.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.210
Is something wrong?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.800
Sagara-senpai has the same mobile phone as Tsuruma-kun?

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.130
Yes.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:44.130
So that means the real identity of the little sister this time is Sagara-sen-

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:48.480
No, it's weird for a senior to be your little sister...

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:51.310
Actually, Sagara-senpai might not be older than I am.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:51.890
Eh?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.840
I didn't believe it myself earlier either,

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:58.280
but she was an abandoned child.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:00.940
What's more, she was found when she was around one or two years old.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:03.330
Her date of birth isn't clear.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:09.830
So that means there's a possibility that she's actually a year older or younger.

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:10.790
That's right.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.540
And if she's actually younger...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:17.540
Who's there?!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.970
I'm a member of the newspaper club.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.130
Oh, it's you again.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:28.720
No matter how many times you ask, I'm not doing an intervie-

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.720
That's not why I'm here!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.970
I'm doing some research today.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:33.310
Research?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:37.650
You and Sagara-senpai are good friends, right?

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.470
Eh?

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:39.060
I guess.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:43.570
Well, about Sagara-senpai closing the café and going back to America...

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:44.990
Do you know anything about it?

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.240
What?!

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:52.490
Actually, it's a rumour that some
students working in Lyrical Sisters heard...

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:55.280
Is this rumour true?

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:58.000
Well, that's what I wanted to ask you...

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:25.990
The love that ran away is searching for Eden

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:37.580
Despite losing my bearings, I understood the weight I felt from you

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:43.210
We felt it on that summer day

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:49.300
Do you regret our meeting because of these painful lies?

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:55.310
Are you saying it was only painful?

00:22:55.310 --> 00:23:02.940
Sweep away the coming tomorrow with those gentle hands

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:09.030
A promise forever from bygone days

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:15.790
We will certainly be together, because I still believe in you

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:21.790
My pounding heart won't stop now

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:27.880
It has finally begun, that lovely thing

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:39.600
To a dazzling world of bewilderment with my heavenly lover

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:44.630
At last, the time for me to do the preview has come!

00:23:44.630 --> 00:23:47.730
The secret power of the king of the black
cats has materialised from the underworld.

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:50.110
All of the girls in the school now have cat ears and tails!

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:53.450
Before long the scent of silver vine will spread and they'll freely groom each other!

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:57.160
All of the world can just roll around and meow all day!

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:00.620
Next time, episode 6: Cat-eared maid little sisters.

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:01.600
Not yet!

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:02.470
It's still too early!

00:24:02.470 --> 00:24:04.420
I'll keep my cat ears suppressed!

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:06.440
Wait, it's not about that at all!

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:09.710
I'm sorry my delusions are such a bother!
